{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1791927706","published":"2026-10-13T21:42:04Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:30:14.667238965Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-1218","CVE-2025-14181","CVE-2026-6103","CVE-2026-91765","CVE-2026-91766","CVE-2026-91767","CVE-2026-91768","CVE-2026-91769","CVE-2026-92842","CVE-2026-93682"],"summary":"Fix of 10 CVEs","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: packet over-reads in the mysqlnd wire protocol parser\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-1218.patch: check the remaining packet size\n       before each read in ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_wireprotocol.c, and check the\n       field length against the field type in ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_ps_codec.c\n     - CVE-2025-1218\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in SOAP HTTP chunked responses\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-14181.patch: use size_t lengths and checked\n       reallocation for the response body in ext/soap/php_http.c\n     - CVE-2025-14181\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: phar tar entry injection via unchecked entry size\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-6103.patch: reject unrepresentable entry sizes\n       and skip the data of every entry type that has data in ext/phar/tar.c\n     - CVE-2026-6103\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: unbounded recursion in SOAP XML parsing and decoding\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91765.patch: walk XML nodes iteratively, reject\n       documents nested deeper than 2048 levels and limit the decoding depth\n       in ext/soap/php_xml.c and ext/soap/php_encoding.c\n     - CVE-2026-91765\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: credentials leaked to another origin on HTTP redirects\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91766.patch: strip the Authorization, Cookie\n       and Proxy-Authorization user headers when a redirect changes the\n       scheme, host or port in ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c\n     - CVE-2026-91766\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap over-read in TLS wildcard certificate name\n     matching\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91767.patch: include the wildcard prefix\n       length in the subject length check in ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c\n     - CVE-2026-91767\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: FastCGI allowed_clients matched IPv6 clients on a /96\n     prefix\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91768.patch: compare the full 16-byte IPv6\n       address in fcgi_is_allowed() in main/fastcgi.c\n     - CVE-2026-91768\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: TLS peer name check fell back to the certificate CN\n     when the certificate has a service identity\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91769.patch: do not fall back to the Common\n       Name when the certificate has a DNS, URI or SRV subjectAltName in\n       ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c\n     - CVE-2026-91769\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap over-read in convert stream filters with a NUL\n     byte in line-break-chars\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-92842.patch: duplicate line-break-chars with\n       pestrndup() in ext/standard/filters.c\n     - CVE-2026-92842\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap over-read on an empty Location header in HTTP\n     redirects\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-93682.patch: use the stored Location length\n       when resolving a relative redirect in\n       ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c\n     - CVE-2026-93682","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libapache2-mod-php7.4","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libapache2-mod-php7.4?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.4.33-1+deb11u12+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1791927706.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libphp7.4-embed","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libphp7.4-embed?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.4.33-1+deb11u12+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1791927706.json"}},{"package":{"name":"php7.4","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare